  "causes": {
    "arches": "Analytic ellipse versus midpoint contour; sample intervals count positions minus one. Midpoint colour cells replace tangent-dependent cap compensation.",
    "cones": "Separate analytic rings use exact original centres/radii. The conic boundary can overwrite different older rings than the midpoint contour. The original radius-1 circle includes the diagonal (1,1): its integer midpoint tie keeps Y unchanged. A true thin circle can miss that corner; the raw geometry budget is 1%.",
    "yarnball": "Original staged integer centres and derived radii; analytic/midpoint contour intersections can expose older ring colours. Sample cells eliminate the former -1 cap lag.",
    "gumballs": "Logical rectangular colour cells clipped to the analytic ellipse. At boundary cells the conic can replace an older ball that the cached raster left visible.",
    "daisies": "Original cached-ray pens plus the approved filled surface. Rays-only diagnostic is exact in shared raw ink; the surface fills moire holes and can cover older flowers through them.",
    "sine": "Native draws the real curve the original truncates to cells, shrunk half a cell toward zero, so it stays within half a cell of each sample. It passes through cell edges the staircase covers, so overlap is low by design; within-cell is the shape guard.",
    "corkscrew": "Native draws the real curve the original truncates to cells, shrunk half a cell toward zero, so it stays within half a cell of each sample. It passes through cell edges the staircase covers, so overlap is low by design; within-cell is the shape guard.",
    "ellipse": "Original integer fan endpoints and midpoint colour cells. At reduced sizes a subpixel sample shift can select a neighbouring ray/colour band.",
    "littleStars": "Original manual sign/swap order and conditional copies. Reduced-grid phase can select a neighbouring ray with a distinct per-copy colour.",
    "bigstar": "Actual cached endpoints, including stale entries. Reduced-grid phase changes which crossing ray covers a pixel; no ideal-star replacement.",
    "boxes": "Exact raw logical-cell ray pens, with omitted terminal sample and separate reset origin. Reduction phase can select an adjacent fan ray.",
    "puffs": "Exact raw ray cells except incidental terminal stores. Sparse thin rays are sensitive to reduction phase, including diagonal nearest neighbours.",
    "bars": "Exact raw parallel segments. Reduced sampling can choose the adjacent shifted segment, normally one ramp index away.",
    "wandering": "Exact raw moving endpoints/segments; reduction phase changes coverage at crossings of differently coloured lines.",
    "squirals": "Exact original integer vertices and edge order, not pre-truncation vertices. Reduced-grid phase changes coverage at adjacent spiral edges.",
    "sweep2": "Exact cyclic ray cells; accelerating instances remain declared Faithful. Reduced sampling can choose an adjacent ray/colour.",
    "hexagon": "Original vertical/diagonal integer runs are exact raw and at 4K; 2x nearest-centre reduction changes coverage at short run endpoints with a 1.2-pixel VGA400 row pitch.",
    "hilbert": "The original line_step path paints overlapping square stamps at each point (width 1, 3 or 6). The Native width stroke partitions connected samples at midpoints, so a few stamp boundaries and per-point overwrite colours differ; 2x adds nearest-row phase changes. EGA XOR instances explicitly fall back.",
    "spiral": "The cardinal integer-step spiral is exact. The 2x preview keeps the same path and has no measured residual.",
    "spiral1": "The growing diamond increments colour before plotting the first point of each new circuit. Overlapping diagonal turn cells then differ by ramp index, with a few Native-only edge cells; 2x adds nearest-row phase changes.",
    "squares": "Cardinal integer circuits are exact raw and at 4K; a few cells at reduced circuit corners differ under 2x nearest-centre sampling.",
    "sweep": "A straight ray with slope 1/run replaces the integer runs the original quantizes it into. Exact-cell overlap falls by design; shift and within-cell guard the figure.",
    "zigstream": "Random integer runs and resets are exact raw and at 4K; the 2x row pitch changes coverage at short turns and resets.",
    "cycloids": "A centripetal spline passes through the table positions the original joins with straight lines, so it bows away from those chords between them, most for a large pen radius. Exact-cell overlap and colour fall by design; shift and within-cell guard the figure.",
    "atom": "Real polar origins before truncation (and before EGA Y division), swept by the original 16-cell horizontal pen. Continuous origins and EGA double quantization change boundary coverage; reduced-grid phase can expose an older pen colour.",
    "balls": "The generating circle and distance rings evaluated at real bitmap coordinates; each sample reveals its cell, and outline cells also take the disc in neighbouring skipped samples.",
    "curves": "Real trigonometric origins before the +4 offset, swept by the original 16-cell horizontal pen. Corresponding sample strips close quantization holes; midpoint old/new colours and changed last-writer coverage differ from the truncated raster. Formula wraps break the path.",
    "diag1": "Straight descending diagonal bands partitioned into sample cells, broken at Y wraps and X resets. Raw and 4K are exact. 2x row phase can select the neighbouring diagonal/coordinate colour.",
    "diag2": "Straight rising diagonal bands partitioned into sample cells, broken at Y wraps and X resets. Raw and 4K are exact. 2x row phase can select a neighbouring colour run.",
    "formula1": "Real modular quadratic evaluated per output pixel. Raw integer coordinates remain exact; nearest physical pixel centres at 4K differ fractionally in Y, moving narrow quadratic bands, especially at large Y. No colour-clock change. Reflection/exchange selects the real symmetric wedge continuously, removing the old overlap strip staircase at the diagonal.",
    "grid": "Thresholded bilinear weave mask; missing-cell corners belong to the closest plotted sample, preserving reveal order and tile colours. Adjacent analytic patches compute cuts from the same global endpoint anchor; a repeated-addition endpoint left physical row gaps in the rejected first span trial.",
    "lines": "Four-sample vertical pens sweep parallelograms between successive base positions; a clamped bounce shares its real endpoint.",
    "lotsadots": "Equal-area physical circles at the unchanged independent random coordinates.",
    "pedals": "Real polar origins swept by the original eight-cell diagonal pen. Straight diagonal bands replace cell staircases; corresponding swept sample strips close the holes between tracks. Changed coverage/older colours and nearest reduction remain visible, with zero shift and one-cell proximity guards.",
    "ribbons": "Per-sample trapezoid slices between walking row ends; random position wraps break the band. Rare raw/4K residuals occur at a wrap or changing run length.",
    "triangles": "Trapezoid slices between walking row bounds, retaining the original horizontal row colour bands.",
    "tunnel": "Straight row bands with a sloping end in the triangular variant; shared side continuations use the same geometry.",
    "sierpinski": "Equal-area physical circles at the unchanged chaos-game visits.",
    "butterflies": "Straight wing polygons. Thin overlaps differ at inclusive Classic boundary cells; isolated outer stores are now round.",
    "diamonds": "Straight polygon boundary and colour-distance contours measured from the real left edge, replacing the stair-stepped row-left colour origin. A fractional ramp origin changes shared raw indices; outer stores are round.",
    "tiles": "Axis-aligned rectangular fill bands and square rectangle corners. These cells already tile the sampled rectangle exactly; only the isolated outer point becomes round.",
    "wedges": "Straight triangular faces and real left-edge colour-distance contours, retaining horizontal row bands. Raw colour changes trace to the fractional left-edge origin."
  },
